{
  "comment": [
    "The objc: package's foreign calls (.kb/objc.md), for rontolisp's own binary and for a compiled",
    "objc: program: a -o X.class/.jar output carries this file under",
    "META-INF/native-image/rontolisp-objc/<program>/, so native-image builds the jar with no",
    "configuration (the bridge's two reflective lookups travel beside it, in rontolisp-objc-bridge).",
    "It stands ALONE, so the FIRST entries repeat shapes the rontolisp file beside this one registers",
    "for the GPU drivers: the objc_msgSend ones -- the Metal driver's selectors, which metal.lisp and",
    "scene.lisp send through objc:send, and the CUDA shapes that coincide with one -- and then the",
    "four C shapes the runtime binds as well, jint() (pthread_main_np), void*()",
    "(objc_autoreleasePoolPush), void*(void*) (objc_getClass, sel_registerName) and void(void*)",
    "(objc_autoreleasePoolPop).",
    "",
    "After them come am.ik.objc's runtime downcalls",
    "(objc_getClass, sel_registerName, class_addMethod, protocol_getMethodDescription with",
    "its struct { SEL; const char* } answer, dispatch_sync_f/dispatch_async_f, pthread_main_np,",
    "CFRunLoopRunInMode / CFRunLoopSourceCreate / CFRunLoopAddSource -- the run loop thread 0 parks in) and then the CLOSED TABLE of objc_msgSend shapes a native image",
    "can serve: the shapes appkit.lisp, metal.lisp, scene.lisp and the documented examples send, plus the 60 most common",
    "shapes of a census over the instance and class methods of 29 core AppKit/Foundation classes",
    "(13,065 methods on macOS 26.3; the top 60 reach 90.6% of them, ObjcRuntime derives a shape from",
    "the selector's own type encoding). The last one is outside the census: it is NSTimer's",
    "scheduledTimerWithTimeInterval:target:selector:userInfo:repeats:, the repeating clock behind",
    "appkit:timer, and the one before it is",
    "performSelectorOnMainThread:withObject:waitUntilDone:, which appkit.lisp uses to start",
    "-[NSApplication run] on thread 0 (without it no click is ever dispatched).",
    "The last FOUR are the system frameworks examples/macos/system-frameworks.lisp reaches past",
    "AppKit, the shapes the census over AppKit and Foundation did not already cover:",
    "NSSpellChecker's checkSpellingOfString:startingAt: (an NSRange answer) and",
    "guessesForWordRange:inString:language:inSpellDocumentWithTag: (an NSRange argument),",
    "NSDataDetector's matchesInString:options:range:, and CIColor's colorWithRed:green:blue:.",
    "The next TWO are Metal's, for examples/macos/metal-triangle.lisp and metal-cube.lisp:",
    "MTLDevice's newBufferWithBytes:length:options: and MTLRenderCommandEncoder's",
    "drawPrimitives:vertexStart:vertexCount:. Everything else those two programs send -- and every",
    "selector objc:data, objc:bytes and the :error out slot send -- the census already covered.",
    "The LAST one is metal:pixels' readback, MTLTexture's",
    "getBytes:bytesPerRow:fromRegion:mipmapLevel: -- an MTLRegion (six NSUIntegers) by value, the",
    "widest struct argument in the table, and the shape a window-free frame is read back through",
    "(.kb/geom.md, \"How the renderer is tested\").",
    "A selector whose shape is outside this table SIGNALS in the",
    "binary, naming the entry to add here; the JVM registers nothing ahead of time and binds any",
    "shape. ObjcNativeImageForeignConfigTest pins the runtime shapes on every machine and the",
    "appkit selectors on a Mac.",
    "",
    "Then 144 VARIADIC objc_msgSend entries: the shapes am.ik.objc.VariadicSelectors' table is",
    "sent through (arrayWithObjects:, stringWithFormat: and the rest of the nil-terminated and",
    "format-string family, whose type encoding is byte for byte their fixed-arity twins'). A",
    "variadic call is its own stub -- on Apple's arm64 ABI a variadic argument travels on the",
    "STACK where a fixed one travels in a register, which is why sending one through the declared",
    "shape kills the process inside objc_retain -- so an entry carries firstVariadicArg and never",
    "answers for the same layouts without it. THREE fixed halves (void*(void*,void*,void*) and",
    "void(void*,void*,void*), both splitting at 3, and void(void*,void*,void*,void*) splitting at 4,",
    "which is +[NSException raise:format:]) crossed with 48 variadic tails: 1 to 12 arguments, every",
    "carrier combination (void*, jlong, jdouble -- what va_arg reads for %@, %ld and %f) up to 4",
    "and void* only past it. The LAST variadic argument is always void*, because the binding",
    "appends the nil terminator itself, which is what keeps the family finite. A wider or more",
    "mixed list -- a fourth numeric format argument, a thirteenth object -- signals with the entry",
    "to add. ObjcNativeImageForeignConfigTest generates this grid from those rules and pins it",
    "against this file in BOTH directions.",
    "",
    "The upcalls are the objc: package's: one entry per",
    "callback shape -- MainThread's trampoline (void(void*)) and ObjcClasses' closed set of IMPs",
    "(a class defined at run time gets a method body that is an upcall stub). An upcall stub, like",
    "a downcall stub, exists in the binary only for a registered shape."
  ],
